    "caption": "The Palme d'Or has a twin. Chopard makes the Cannes trophy in Geneva. It begins as a small palm sculpted in blue wax. Plaster is baked around it until the wax melts out, then molten gold is poured into the empty shape. The palm has 19 leaves and a tiny heart on its stem, and holds about 118 grams of 18 carat gold. It stands on a base of rock crystal, and no two crystals match, so each year's trophy looks different. One trophy takes more than 40 hours of handwork. Every year Chopard also makes a spare, in case of a tie.",
